# 9. The Ultimate Memory Diagram

```text
                         MAP
                          │
              ┌───────────┴───────────┐
              │                       │
          Interface              Implementations
                                      │
       ┌──────────────┬───────────────┼───────────────┬──────────────┬──────────────┐
       │              │               │               │              │              │
    HashMap     LinkedHashMap     TreeMap        Hashtable   ConcurrentHashMap  WeakHashMap
       │              │               │               │              │              │
    General       Insertion       Sorted          Legacy        Concurrent       Weak keys
     purpose       order           keys         synchronized      access
```

## One-line exam memory

> **HashMap → general, LinkedHashMap → insertion order, TreeMap → sorted keys, Hashtable → legacy synchronized, ConcurrentHashMap → concurrent access, WeakHashMap → weak keys.**

**And, as required for your training notes, none of these examples uses Generics.**
